  newspaper:
    masthead: SEOUL DAILY
    issue: No. 12,408
    dateLine: TUESDAY, OCTOBER 6, 2026
    price: 1,000 won
    headline: Holiday "gas bill" calls were fake
    subhead: Residents who checked their bill and their bank history hung up.
    photo: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 4c63c0d2cf38942db834f06de02c655f, type: 3}
    caption: 'Before any transfer, the bank shows who really gets the money. Photo:
      Seoul Daily'
    body:
    - A woman calling herself "Team Leader Baek" of Mapo City Gas's billing team
      phoned residents of Mangwon-dong on Monday's holiday. She said their September
      gas bill was unpaid, and that the gas would be shut off at five unless they
      transferred the money at once.
    - Most of those called had already paid by automatic transfer. Police say the
      account she gave, Hanbit Bank 620-339-104772, is in the name of a man in his
      twenties who sold it to the ring. Anyone called by 010-7359-2046 can report
      it to 112 or the fraud hotline 1332.
    - '"We do not phone customers to collect bills, and our offices were closed for
      the holiday," Mapo City Gas said. "Our only number is 02-555-0181, the one
      printed on the bill."'
    warningTitle: SELLING SECOND-HAND? READ YOUR OWN BANK
    warningText: '"I paid you too much, send back the difference" is an honest slip
      on some days and a trick on others, and the buyer''s name and account can be
      real either way. A transfer arrives within seconds. Only your own bank history
      shows whether the money came, and from whom.'
    print: {fileID: 0}
    local:
    - title: Gas inspections next week
      text: Mapo City Gas checks villas in Mangwon-dong from 12 Oct. Inspectors carry
        ID and never collect money.
    - title: Water tank cleaning
      text: Several villas on Poeun-ro will be without water on Thursday morning.
    - title: Subway fares
      text: The base fare stays at 1,550 won through the end of the year.
    ads:
    - title: "\uCE58\uD0A8 CHICKEN 24H"
      text: Crispy & soy garlic. Free delivery over 20,000 won. 02-555-0147
    - title: CHECKFIRST.KR
      text: Who owns that number? Whose account is it? Look it up before you send.
    - title: HANBIT ACADEMY
      text: TOEIC weekend class, 30% off for students. 02-555-0166
  drawer:
  - title: "Lease contract \xB7 Unit 302"
    kind: 0
    issuer: Mangwon Heights
    fields:
    - label: Landlord
      value: Choi Youngsik
      isFact: 0
      factKind: 6
    - label: Landlord's phone
      value: 010-5512-3380
      isFact: 1
      factKind: 0
    - label: Rent
      value: 450,000 won a month, due on the 7th
      isFact: 0
      factKind: 6
    - label: Rent account
      value: 110-771-209944
      isFact: 1
      factKind: 1
    - label: Account holder
      value: Choi Youngsik (Nuri Bank)
      isFact: 0
      factKind: 6
    - label: If absent, contact
